<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down, oil, meal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down, oil, meal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained bearish in central Indian markets on limited demand from processing plants on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were down by 100-150 rupees per tonne. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were almost steady in very thin trading today. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady and soymeal yellow was quoted at $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) at west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $95-96 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,275-3,300 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Rapeseed extraction prices were down today.</p>
